-- Seed public.soundtracks / public.soundtrack_songs from sound/soundtracks.json.
--
-- A one-time lift of the file that was the source of truth until 2026-07-29:
-- 69 city tapes, 929 songs, verbatim. Positions are the songs' order in the
-- file, so the tapes play exactly as they did before the move.
--
-- Read the JSON as UTF-8 if you ever regenerate this. The first version of this
-- file was generated on Windows with Python's locale encoding (cp1252), which
-- turned every non-ASCII character into its double-encoded twin — 'Tiesto' with
-- a diaeresis arrived as two characters, in 92 fields across 24 cities. Fixed by
-- 2026072907_soundtracks_encoding_repair.sql; this file is the corrected source.
--
-- Idempotent: tapes upsert on city_slug, songs do nothing on the
-- (city_slug, title, artist) unique index, so re-running cannot duplicate a
-- track or reorder a tape a human has since edited. It will NOT undo an
-- archive/restore done after the move — that is deliberate.

on conflict (city_slug) do update set
  spine_tag = coalesce(soundtracks.spine_tag, excluded.spine_tag),
  spine_tag_position = coalesce(soundtracks.spine_tag_position, excluded.spine_tag_position);

on conflict do nothing;
